$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-2})+(\goldD{-4})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-3}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f(\blueD{-3})$:

$\begin{align}
f(\blueD{-3})&=(\blueD{-3})^2+6(\blueD{-3})+8
\\\\
&=9-18+8
\\\\
&=-1
\end{align}$
